## 3. Architecture (critical — security & network)

> **عربي:** ليه المتصفح مش بيتصل بالـ SQL لوحده

### 3.1 Why not “browser talks TDS/Postgres directly”

Browsers cannot safely open raw SQL Server/Postgres sockets to private servers. Customer DBs are almost always on **LAN / VPN / allowlisted IPs** — not public internet. A cloud-only proxy that holds customer SQL passwords is a **high-risk** design and often blocked by firewalls.

> **عربي:** قرار: الكونكت الحي على الديسكتوب أولًا

### 3.2 Phased decision (LOCKED for planning)

| Phase | Where live SQL connect runs | Same features? |
|-------|----------------------------|----------------|
| **Phase 1 (primary)** | **Desktop only** (Tauri + sidecar connector on LAN/VPN) | Full: connect, catalog, run SQL, schema-aware chat |
| **Phase 1 web role** | Web = **same Support UI + chat history** (Firestore); Connect button uses **desktop bridge / “Open in Desktop”** when user is browser-only | UX parity for chat/history/profiles metadata — **not** raw sockets from the browser |
| **Later (Phase 2+)** | Optional **browser-only live connect** via on-prem **Vigil DB Gateway** (customer VPC) or approved tunnel | Aim for feature parity with desktop connector API |

**Answer in product terms:**  
- نعم، الشغل **الأساسي للـ Connect الحي** = **الديسكتوب**.  
- الويب يبقى فيه نفس وضع Support والشاتس والبروفايلات، ويتصل **من خلال** الديسكتوب (embed/bridge) في المرحلة الأولى.  
- **كونكت كامل من المتصفح لوحده بنفس الفيتشز** = **لاحقاً** (مش Phase 1)، عشان الفايروول والأمان.

```text
┌─────────────────────────────┐
│ Vigil Web (User shell)      │  Chat UI, Support mode, history (Firestore)
│  - Connection profiles UX   │  Metadata only in cloud (optional)
│  - Schema tree (via bridge) │  Live tree only when Desktop/Gateway connected
└──────────────┬──────────────┘
               │ auth + UI (+ optional embed)
┌──────────────▼──────────────┐
│ Vigil Desktop / local       │  ★ LIVE CONNECTOR — Phase 1 primary
│ connector (Tauri sidecar)   │  - User enters server, db, user, password
│  - SQL Server (tedious/mssql)│  - Credentials in OS keychain / local vault
│  - PostgreSQL (pg)          │  - Introspect + execute on LAN/VPN
└──────────────┬──────────────┘
               │ results / schema snapshots (bounded)
               ▼
         Agent context (no full DB dump to Firestore)
```

- [x] **Phase 1:** Desktop owns the live connection.  
- [x] **Phase 1 web:** same Support shell; browser-alone → **Open in Vigil Desktop to connect** (or embed already running on desktop).  
- [ ] **Later:** on-prem **Vigil DB Gateway** for true browser-only teams — same connector API; still no raw passwords in Firestore.  
- [ ] **Never** put SQL passwords in Firestore plaintext.  
- [ ] Optional cloud fields: connection **display name**, host nickname, engine type, last-used — **not** secrets.  
- [ ] Schema snapshots sent to the model must be **bounded** (selected DB/schema, top-N objects, summaries) — never “upload whole production DB.”  
- [ ] Query **result grids** stay local/session by default; user may pin a small excerpt into chat deliberately.

