### 5.1 SQL Activity Capture — “Vigil Profiler” (CRITICAL for support)

**Problem today:** To know which SQL runs when the desktop EXE opens a report or a button is clicked, support opens **SQL Server Profiler** (or traces), hunts **SPIDs / filters / Application Name**, clicks in the app, then digs the batch out. Slow, error-prone, tool-outside-Vigil.

**Product answer:** Yes — using the **same SQL connection** Vigil already has (plus permissions). We do **not** embed the old Profiler UI. We implement a **Support-friendly Activity Capture** panel powered by modern SQL Server observability:

| Technique | Role | Needs |
|-----------|------|--------|
| **DMVs (live)** | What’s running *right now*: `sys.dm_exec_requests` + `sys.dm_exec_sql_text` + `sys.dm_exec_connections` / sessions | `VIEW SERVER STATE` (or equivalent) |
| **DMVs (recent)** | What just finished (plan cache): `sys.dm_exec_query_stats` + sql_text — good for short bursts | Same |
| **Extended Events (preferred capture)** | Time-boxed ring buffer / file target: `sql_batch_completed`, `rpc_completed`, `sql_statement_completed` filtered by login / host / app_name / database / spid | CREATE EVENT SESSION (or use a pre-deployed Vigil session template) |
| **Query Store** (if on) | Historical regressions per DB — complement, not click-sync | Query Store enabled |
| **Legacy Profiler traces** | Avoid as default (deprecated); only if customer mandates | — |

**Not required:** User manually opening Profiler, copying SPID into a form as the happy path.

#### Support UX (make it addictive)

- [ ] Panel: **Activity / Profiler** under Support / DB  
- [ ] Modes:
  - **Watch live** — poll DMVs every N ms; show running requests (spid, login, host, app, db, wait, elapsed, sql text preview)
  - **Capture window** — Start → user clicks in EXE / opens report → Stop → list batches/RPCs captured (duration, reads, cpu, text)
  - **Filter presets:** my login, this host, Application Name contains `…`, database = X, exclude Vigil’s own spid  
- [ ] One-click **“Capture next click”** when Desktop EXE Runtime is attached: Start XEvents/DMV window → optional `app_click` / user clicks → Stop → show SQL tied to that action  
- [ ] Click a captured statement → full text editor, **Explain**, “Add to ticket”, “Open related objects” (parse proc names)  
- [ ] AI: «الجملة دي بطيئة ليه؟» / «منين التقرير بيجيب البيانات؟» grounded in captured text + schema  
- [ ] Arabic labels: «بدء الالتقاط» / «إيقاف» / «الجمل أثناء فتح التقرير»

#### Correlate with Desktop EXE (killer combo)

```text
User: "افتح تقرير المبيعات وورّيني جملة السيكوال"
  → optional app_* navigate / user opens report
  → Activity Capture window (2–15s)
  → show top SQL by duration / by time order
  → pin into chat + ticket evidence
```

See `05-اختبار-برامج-EXE-ويندوز.mdc` §13.1 — keep both specs in sync.

#### Filters that replace “خذ رقم الـ session”

- [ ] Auto-detect **Application Name** from EXE connection string / config-beside-EXE (consent) when possible  
- [ ] Filter by **HostName** = support machine  
- [ ] Filter by **Login** used by the ERP  
- [ ] Optional: user pastes SPID only as power escape hatch — not the default tutorial  

#### Safety & permissions

- [ ] Capture is **observability**, still on the Support connection — document required grants  
- [ ] Default: **do not** capture forever; max duration + row cap (e.g. 30s / 200 events)  
- [ ] Exclude Vigil’s own diagnostic queries from the list (filter by program_name = Vigil)  
- [ ] Captured SQL may contain PII — local/session default; pin deliberately to ticket  
- [ ] Creating XEvent sessions may need DBA one-time setup: ship **script template** “grant + create VigilSupportCapture” for admins  
- [ ] Read-only support users: DMV watch may work with VIEW SERVER STATE; XEvent create may need DBA — degrade gracefully to DMV-only mode with clear message  

#### Implementation sketch (when executing)

- [ ] Tools: `sql_activity_live`, `sql_capture_start`, `sql_capture_stop`, `sql_capture_list`  
- [ ] Prefer XEvents ring_buffer for short captures; fall back to DMV sampling loop  
- [ ] Parse `rpc_completed` object_name + statement for procs Crystal/EXE love  

