### 7.2 Ticket quality bar (what “محترمة” means)

Vigil proposes a strong default template (AR/EN); engineer tweaks; then publish:

| Block | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| **Title** | Short, searchable, developer-facing |
| **Type** | Bug / Task / User Story / Spike (maps to ADO work item type) |
| **Summary** | 2–4 sentences: what’s broken / needed |
| **Business / user impact** | Who feels it, severity |
| **Environment** | DB engine, server nickname, app module, customer (no secrets) |
| **Steps to reproduce** | Numbered |
| **Expected vs actual** | Clear contrast |
| **Evidence** | Queries run (sanitized), error text, object names (`dbo.X`), screenshots links if any |
| **Suspected area** | Tables/procs/reports touched — from live DB session when available |
| **Acceptance criteria** | Bullets developers can check off |
| **Out of scope / notes** | Optional |
| **Priority / Severity** | P0–P3 + Sev |

- [ ] AI fills from **current Support chat + DB context** so the engineer doesn’t re-type the investigation  
- [ ] Engineer can say “اختصر” / “زود تفاصيل للـ DBA” / “خليها Task مش Bug” and regenerate sections  
- [ ] Output is scannable **bullets + short paragraphs** — not a wall of chat dump

> **عربي:** قسم — 7.3 Azure DevOps — primary publish target (APIs: YES)

### 7.3 Azure DevOps — primary publish target (APIs: YES)

**Answer:** Azure DevOps exposes a full **Work Item Tracking REST API**. You do **not** have to only create tickets by clicking in their website. Vigil can create work items from outside after the support engineer authorizes their account.

- Create: `POST https://dev.azure.com/{org}/{project}/_apis/wit/workitems/${type}?api-version=7.2`  
  Body: JSON Patch fields (`System.Title`, `System.Description`, `Microsoft.VSTS.TCM.ReproSteps`, tags, Area Path, Iteration, Assigned To, …)  
- ADO assigns the **next work item ID** automatically on create — Vigil shows `#1234` + deep link back.  
- Auth options:
  - **Preferred for product:** **Microsoft Entra ID OAuth** per user (each support engineer signs in with their ADO/Entra account — “extension-like” connect once). Legacy Azure DevOps OAuth is deprecated for new apps (2025+); use Entra.  
  - **Fallback / enterprise:** Personal Access Token (PAT) stored in OS keychain — simpler but orgs increasingly restrict PATs.  
- Permissions: user’s own ADO identity creates the item (audit trail = that engineer), subject to project permissions.

**Vigil UX for ADO link**
- [ ] Settings → **Integrations → Azure DevOps**: Connect account (Entra OAuth)  
- [ ] Choose default **Organization**, **Project**, default work item type (Bug/Task), Area Path  
- [ ] Per-ticket override before publish  
- [ ] On success: save `adoWorkItemId`, URL, title on the Vigil ticket draft; status → `published`  
- [ ] Optional: attach truncated evidence as Discussion comment via API  

**Not required:** embedding the full Azure DevOps website as the only create path (may still deep-link to open the item after publish).

