## 13. Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Support engineer can enter SQL Server host/user/password, connect, see databases/tables/views  
- [ ] Ask in Arabic/English “ليه التقرير بيكسر على جدول X؟” and get an answer using **live** columns — without pasting schema by hand  
- [ ] Same for PostgreSQL  
- [ ] Support can **Start/Stop capture** around opening a report or an EXE click and see the SQL text **without SQL Profiler**  
- [ ] After investigation, engineer asks for a ticket → gets a **structured, editable** draft with repro + acceptance criteria  
- [ ] With ADO connected, **Publish** creates a work item via API and returns `#id` + URL (no mandatory manual form on ado.microsoft.com)  
- [ ] Dedicated **Tickets** area lists drafts/published  
- [ ] Read-only blocks `DROP` without explicit write mode + confirm  
- [ ] SQL secrets + ADO tokens not stored in Firestore  
- [ ] Usage meters on the same account wallet  
- [ ] Cursor-style paste loop is no longer required for the happy path  

